      <section id="about">
        <h2>About</h2>

        <p>
          I am a Project Assistant Professor at Keio University and a
          Ph.D. student at the Graduate School of Media and Governance,
          Keio University.
        </p>

        <p>
          My research focuses on computer networks, particularly mobile
          networks and edge computing. I am interested in designing network
          architectures that integrate mobile networks and computing
          infrastructure for 5G and beyond.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="research">
        <h2>Research</h2>

        <div class="research-item">
          <h3>Mobile &amp; Edge Computing</h3>
          <p>
            Network architectures that integrate mobile networks and
            edge computing environments, including Multi-access Edge
            Computing (MEC).
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="research-item">
          <h3>5G / 6G Networks</h3>
          <p>
            User-plane architectures, network control, and resource
            placement for current and future mobile networks.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="research-item">
          <h3>Geo-distributed Networks</h3>
          <p>
            Design, operation, and measurement of geo-distributed
            network infrastructure.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

